cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use bindingsite for a figure or an analysis, please cite it as below."
title: "bindingsite: binding-site figures in one PyMOL command"
abstract: >-
  A PyMOL plugin that turns a protein-ligand complex into a finished
  binding-site view: ligand, pocket residues, colour-coded non-covalent and
  covalent interactions perceived from heavy-atom geometry, residue labels that
  do not overlap, a colour key and an automatically chosen camera.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Bonus
    given-names: Michele
    affiliation: "Heinrich Heine University Düsseldorf"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-11-27"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/MicheleBonus/pymol-bindingsite"
url: "https://github.com/MicheleBonus/pymol-bindingsite"
keywords:
  - PyMOL
  - plugin
  - protein-ligand interactions
  - binding site
  - molecular visualization
  - structure-based drug design
